  ],
  "text": "South America and Africa fit together because they used to be the same coastline. Every child notices it. For fifty years no scientist was allowed to say it. Then came fossils of the same animal on both sides of an ocean it could never cross. Because there was no ocean. There was one enormous continent. Then it tore, and the pieces have been drifting apart ever since. But nobody could explain what was doing the pushing. Heat from the core makes the rock below circle, like water in a pan. The plates just ride on top of it. A few centimetres a year, which sounds like nothing at all. But India has been driving into Asia for fifty million years. That collision is Everest, and it is still climbing a few millimetres a year. The map on your wall is a photograph, not a fact. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
